candidates.mechanism:
Phase 3 of execute_batch_phases (native_executor.rs:7611-7714) builds every market's matching input serially on the exec thread before the books go to the pool. Per prepared order it does:
- an insert into ReduceOnlyPositions (a HashMap with no presize, so it rehashes);
- an AccountMargins get plus insert or insert_taker_only (also a HashMap with no presize);
- taker_margin_limit (an Arc clone plus reserve_price);
- a push into the MatchRequest Vec.
Per market it also calls reduce_only_positions_for, margin_tiers and set_mark.

Every input is read-only and belongs to one market:
- the AccountReader is Sync (MakerAccountSource: Sync) and the match workers already share it;
- markets, pools, margin_configs and market_batches are immutable here, and pass A already shares market_batches with pool jobs.

With TORUS_PARALLEL_MATCH_PREP=1:
- The exec thread only takes the books, and creates the rare missing book from market_shape.
- A new MarketWorkerPool entry point takes a Sync per-market prep closure. Each job builds its market's ReduceOnlyPositions and AccountMargins, presized to prepared.len(), and its requests in the same per-market order, then calls match_market.
- Optionally the job also clears both maps after matching and returns the charged-maker-fill count, which takes those drops off the exec thread.

