candidates.mechanism:
cf_native_pending holds every native-action body ever seen (~11.9 KB average value), keyed by random 32-byte hashes. It is append-only:
- the pruner never touches it (pruner.rs covers bodies, headers, receipts, trades, status, core-writer and meta only);
- NativeDaStore::remove has no production caller.

With leveled compaction (LZ4, ZSTD bottommost, dynamic level bytes; db.rs:794-809), every L0 flush overlaps the whole key range. Compaction therefore keeps rewriting all body bytes: decompress, merge, ZSTD recompress, with read and write I/O.

Under TORUS_DA_BLOB_FILES=1 the consensus DB's cf_native_pending would use:
- set_enable_blob_files(true), set_min_blob_size(~4 KB, so 400-order places go to blobs and tiny cancels stay inline);
- set_blob_file_size(256 MiB);
- set_blob_compression_type(Zstd by default, about space-neutral with today's bottommost ZSTD; LZ4 as an arm);
- set_enable_blob_gc(false).

Values are then written once, at flush, into blob files, and compaction only moves keys plus ~20 B blob indexes.

Reads are unchanged:
- get_batch_timed and missing() go through batched_multi_get_cf;
- the serve path uses multi_get;
- most recent bodies are still served from the memtable.

All of this is in rust-rocksdb 0.24 (db_options.rs:3460-3545).

candidates.evidence:
Sampler, hsdb-300m-r2-B (main code):
- consensus-DB compaction_cpu is 0.18-0.20 cores per node vs 0.06 for the state DB, i.e. ~76% of the node's compaction CPU;
- rocksdb:low threads use 0.256-0.272 cores per node (io-threads);
- consensus compaction writes 11.7-12.2 MB/s and reads 12.6-13.1 MB/s.

Compaction writes rise across the cell as the CF grows: per 100 s, 4.7 -> 11.9 -> 7.6 -> 18.2 -> 14.1 -> 16.3-19.4 MB/s.

rocksdb-consensus-LOG per CF (3 nodes):
- cf_native_pending: 40-42 compactions, 8.2-8.6 GB in / 7.4-7.7 GB out per cell;
- cf_consensus_meta: 0.02-0.045 GB;
- DA flushes: 117-121 files, 1.77-1.83 GB, from 11.1-11.5 GB raw.
Compaction writes ~4.3x what flush writes, and it is near-pure rewrite (p3s0cf memory 5875672747243702 found the same for the append CFs).

The DA CF grows by ~1.8 GB flushed per node per 10 min at 300m, with no retention.

