result.summary:
Not refuted. The premise holds on main a44000e0. The bench pins TORUS_HASH_ONLY_PUSH_THRESHOLD=8000000 (devnet/wsl/env.sh:45, present in all 3 nodes' environments in hsdb-300m-r2-B) and native gossip is on (main.rs:180-192, start-node.sh:59). So every follower ingests every action twice. Per cell, each follower receives 1,202-1,206 full-body batches carrying 468-471k actions (390 per batch, 4.9-5.6 MB). Gossip delivers every action with 0 drops: each node publishes 235.5k and receives 471.2k. The push is therefore pure duplication: trust-cache misses (471,202) match gossip received (471,199), and hits (1,177,549) are the push copies (470,627) plus about 707k exec lookups. In the code, each duplicate pays the full cost before it is rejected: a deep clone, a DA put_batch (re-hash, bincode, WAL write), the verified_cache_key Keccak, and compute_action_hash plus serialized_size under the pool write lock.

I recomputed the gain from measured data rather than the candidate's estimate. It comes to -0.20 to -0.26 cores per node, the same range as claimed:
- gossip-verify: duplicates are 15-18.5% of its 0.94-0.97 cores (perf profile from build d3cba5e2, same shape, same 1:1 duplicate pattern, ingest path unchanged since);
- consensus DB: push copies are 40% of WAL bytes and 40% of memtable bytes, which drives L0-triggered compactions;
- tokio threads: zstd, borsh and bincode decode of the pushed batches;
- minus the cost of building the manifest.

That gives CPU-s/1M -3.8% to -4.9%, easily resolvable, and device writes -12 to -15 MB/s per node. None of this work runs on the exec thread, which is the bottleneck at 300m (busy 0.995, queue 60 of 66). So matched/s, native blk/s, exec block_ms, block p99 and RSS do not move beyond noise (matched/s +0.1-0.3% from less host contention). It is a CPU and I/O item only, and a bench setting change rather than a code speedup: the compiled production default (512 KB) already sends manifests at these body sizes. Small factual errors: there were 2 manifests per node (in warm-up), not 0. Step 2a's 'skip the deep clone' is not free, because the clone becomes the block body.
